# GLM-5.3-Flash 4 bpw on ONE DGX Spark (TP=1): Mia's AI Lab's EXL3 4bpw (Mia-AiLab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-4bpw-TensorFold,
# rev 76c0b517) - the 3.5bpw checkpoint with every routed expert at 4 bits - with its non-expert
# weights served as FP8 (32 x 32 block scales) and 60% of the routed experts resident, the rest read
# on demand from one pack. No PEER: one box. The checkpoint the author serves and recommends for
# Flash, from use; the one measurement made on one box says otherwise (GLM_SLOTS below).
# 3.5bpw: configs/glm53-flash-35-tp1.env.example. Two Sparks: configs/glm53-flash-40-tp2.env.example.
# Start: cp configs/glm53-flash-40-tp1.env.example .env.glm53-flash-40, edit the paths, then
# scripts/tide.sh start .env.glm53-flash-40    Stop: scripts/tide.sh stop
#
# Setup (docs/glm-flash.md): ~180 GB of disk, nothing else downloaded
#   python3 tools/glm_fetch_dense.py --repo Mia-AiLab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-4bpw-TensorFold --revision 76c0b5173166d2795dd48860f45d8224817f894c \
#       --out <dense dir>                                                   # 19 GB, the non-expert tensors
#   uv run --no-project --with numpy python tools/glm_pack_exl3.py --world 1 --resume --verify 64 \
#       --repo Mia-AiLab/GLM-5.3-Flash-EXL3-4bpw-TensorFold --revision 76c0b5173166d2795dd48860f45d8224817f894c \
#       --out <packs dir>/glm-flash-40-r0of1.bin                            # 156 GB, straight from the Hub
GLM_MODEL_DIR=/home/you/models/GLM-5.3-Flash-4bpw-dense
PORT=8000
SERVED_MODEL_NAME=glm-5.3-flash
GLM_MAX_SEQ=327680
# requests served at once over one paged KV pool (each lane ~0.74 GB: its KDA state 0.3, the state at
# its last prompt's end for the next turn 0.3, rollback rows 0.07)
GLM_LANES=2
GLM_LANE_CHUNK=1024
GLM_KV=fp8
GLM_KV_SPLIT=0
# a memory budget in 3-bit records at Flash's dims (9.47 MB each; this checkpoint's are all 4-bit,
# 12.6 MB). 9700: 7,282 experts resident (60.2%, 91.9 GB) where 3.5bpw keeps 8,341 (69.0%) in the same
# memory. The two measured on this box from one frozen routing history (2026-11-13, docs/glm-flash.md):
# held-out NLL 1.7592 for 3.5bpw's 1.7510 (+0.0082 +- 0.0027 paired: worse), decode picks missed
# 4.0-4.2% (prose) and 12.5-14.3% (code) for 2.0-2.2% and 7.2-9.1%, prose -5.4%, code -1.8%. Recommended
# all the same, by the author's choice after serving both: that is against this measurement, not from
# a newer one (answers were not scored). The box idles at ~7.3 GiB MemAvailable (two lanes, 327,680
# positions, the KV pool allocated whole at boot). Each 1 GB is ~110 slots; memguard stops the server
# under 4 GiB.
GLM_SLOTS=9700
GLM_FLASH_DENSE=fp8
GLM_EXPERT_FORMAT=exl3
GLM_EXL3_DIR=/home/you/models/glm-flash-packs
GLM_EXL3_PACK=/packs/glm-flash-40-r{rank}of1.bin
GLM_HEAD=exl3
GLM_KVB_FP8=1
GLM_EMBED_8BIT=int8
GLM_CHUNK=2048
GLM_PREFILL_REDUCE=bf16
# the routing history: its own state file (never GLM-5.3's), seeded at first boot from GLM_STATS_DB.
# It is the router's, not the experts': 3.5bpw's history and seed serve this checkpoint as they are
# (copy glm-flash-stats.npz to this name to carry yours over)
RUST_GLM_STATE_DB=/home/you/tidelm-rust-state/glm-flash-40-stats.npz
# the bundled seed, read only when the state file does not exist yet: v1 is a day of serving on the
# development box (2.9M routed rows: chat, benches, long-prompt tests; profiles/glm53-flash-history-v1.json).
# v0 (150K tokens of this repo's sources, prefill only) placed a 69% residency over 74.6% of that
# traffic's routed weight against 84.2% placed by the traffic itself. Without a seed, residency starts
# uniform and the output degrades (docs/glm-flash.md). To start over from it: README, "Resetting the
# routing history".
GLM_STATS_DB=/app/profiles/glm53-flash-history-v1.npz
# the disk prefix store holds KV rows, not KDA's state: off (the engine skips it for this model)
GLM_PREFIX_DISK=0
# MTP: up to 7 drafts a round, the chain stopped on the calibrated acceptance (GLM-5.3's setting, its
# prior table learned on from Flash's own rounds). On 3.5bpw, bench.py 2026-11-12, one boot an arm from the same
# state file, 9700 slots, median of 3: prose 22.12 tok/s against 20.27 for depth 3 without a gate
# (+9.1%; runs 22.07-22.28 / 20.15-20.57), code 28.15 against 28.40 (-0.9%, within its spread
# 27.67-28.64); depth 5 with the gate 21.51 / 27.81. Fewer tokens a step (prose 2.01 against 2.17)
# in cheaper rounds: the gate leaves out the rows that would be rejected.
GLM_MTP=1
GLM_MTP_DEPTH=7
GLM_MTP_CAL=0.36
GLM_MTP_DYN=0.9
# the MTP draft passes score a listed vocabulary, not all 154,880 ids (a draft pass 3.64 -> 1.94 ms; a
# token outside the list is only a rejected draft). Built in: 57,344 ids ranked on English chat, code,
# agent traces and Japanese, 235 MB; a lane whose recent text is more than 4% outside the list drafts
# over every id as before (docs/glm-flash.md). GLM_DRAFT_VOCAB=all turns the list off; a path names
# another ranking (tools/build_glm_draft_vocab.py builds one for your languages).
#GLM_DRAFT_VOCAB=all
#GLM_DRAFT_VOCAB_ROWS=57344
GLM_COPY=1
GLM_LOOKUP=8
GLM_ADAPT=1
GLM_ADAPT_EVERY=200
GLM_ADAPT_PREFILL_SWAPS=512
GLM_ADAPT_DECODE_SWAPS=256
GLM_HOT=1
GLM_HOT_KEEP=32
GLM_HOT_ASYNC=1
# Inline rescue (GLM_HOT_ASYNC=1 only): a decode pass runs as its segments, and a missed pick carrying
# >= 0.4 of its row's routed weight is read into the transient slot before its layer's MoE and computed
# exactly, then kept over a queued victim as a hot read is: the heavy first occurrence covered in the
# pass that missed it, not the one after (docs/hot-predict.md). Measured on 3.5bpw's profile (2026-11-13, two
# boots from one state file, heldout quick + eval teacher-forced, 57,315 tokens): 728 rescues (0.10 a
# pass), decode passes +0.0 to +0.2% (bench-ab, 1-16 rows), the NLL run 1,069 s vs 1,095 s off; NLL
# 1.7121 -> 1.7169 (+0.0048 +- 0.0015 paired, coding +0.0120, no blown windows). A numerics-neutral
# perturbation through the same harness (fp32 attention partials: the boots' hot reads diverge the
# same way) moved it +0.0006 +- 0.0012: the loss is rescue's own, cause not found. On since 2026-11-13
# all the same, by the author's choice (every profile with async hot reads runs it): that is against
# this measurement, not from a newer one. 0: off.
GLM_HOT_RESCUE=0.4
GLM_BG=1
GLM_BG_EVERY=2
GLM_REASONING_EFFORT=low
GLM_DEFAULT_MAX_TOKENS=32768
# image input: the checkpoint's vision tower (1.13 GB) loaded on demand into expert slots lent for
# the request, so text-only traffic keeps the memory for experts; an image is resized to at most
# this many tokens (one a 28 x 28 pixel cell; the processor's own cap, 8000). A request carries any
# number of images: their features (8 KB a token) are allocated for its prefill, and a follow-up
# turn reuses the prefix past the images it shares with the lane's sequence
GLM_VISION=1
GLM_VISION_MAX_TOKENS=8000
